body:
Implements code display components following [Cloudflare's documentation style guide](https://developers.cloudflare.com/style-guide/components/github-code/) and adopts standard Cloudflare Workers patterns throughout the codebase.

## Components

- **GitHubCode**: Fetches and displays code directly from GitHub repos with line filtering, numbers, collapsing, and wrapping
- **CodeBlock**: Inline code blocks with syntax highlighting placeholders, line highlighting, and collapsible sections
- Both components: Full RTL/Arabic support, dark mode, accessibility compliance

```tsx
// Usage in Astro pages
<GitHubCode
  client:load
  repo="llu77/-lmm"
  path="src/index.ts"
  startLine={10}
  endLine={30}
  showLineNumbers
/>

<CodeBlock
  lang="typescript"
  highlight={[3, 4, 5]}
  showLineNumbers
>
  {code}
</CodeBlock>
```

## Workers Pattern

Standardized worker entry points following Cloudflare's exported handler pattern:

```typescript
// src/types/cloudflare.ts - Type definitions
export interface Env {
  KV?: KVNamespace;
  DB?: D1Database;
  BUCKET?: R2Bucket;
  AI?: Ai;
}

// Standard worker pattern
export default {
  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext): Promise<Response> {
    try {
      await env.KV?.put("KEY", "VALUE");
      const value = await env.KV?.get("KEY");
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ value }), {
        headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }
      });
    } catch (error) {
      return new Response(
        JSON.stringify({ error: error.message }),
        { status: 500, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } }
      );
    }
  }
};
```

## Code Formatting Standards

- Placeholders: `<SECRET_NAME>` (angle brackets)
- Optional params: `[OPTIONS]` (square brackets)  
- Shell commands: No `$` prefix
- Inline code: Backticks for files, commands, values

## Documentation

- Arabic style guide for Workers patterns (KV, D1, R2 examples)
- Component usage guide with 12+ examples
- Interactive examples page at `/code-examples`
- Quick reference for common patterns

